@startuml clinical-workflow-current
' Current ICU workflow without the system — DIP-27
' Source of diagrams/export/clinical-workflow-current.png
' Based on MoH Order No. 78 (2023), the national sepsis protocol (2020) and respondents R1, R2 (transcripts.md).
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #444444
}
skinparam swimlane {
  TitleFontStyle bold
}

title Current workflow in an ICU (without the system)

|Bedside monitor|
start
:Measures vital signs continuously;
|ICU nurse|
:Reads the monitor and charts values\n(ICU: every hour; ward: every 4–8 h);
:Watches several patients\n(about one nurse per two ICU beds);
if (Notices a change?) then (yes)
  :Checks the patient:\nconsciousness, vital signs;
  if (Significant?) then (yes)
    :Informs the physician;
    |Physician|
    :Assesses with the national sepsis protocol\n(qSOFA / SOFA);
    :Lactate and blood cultures within 1.5 h,\nfluids, antibiotics, source control;
  else (no)
    |ICU nurse|
    :Continues routine observation;
  endif
else (no / missed)
  |ICU nurse|
  :Change not recognised in time;
  note right
    Weak points named by both respondents:
    early signs taken as minor, changes lost
    at handover or at night, many patients,
    physician not available at once.
  end note
endif
stop
@enduml
